WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:08.884
Hold on.

2
00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:10.761
Let me take a look.

3
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.269
Jian. are you back from school?

4
00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:21.813
JIAN
17 YEARS OLD

5
00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:31.448
The house is perfectly fine.
Why are you breaking it down?

6
00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.992
This house is not perfectly fine.

7
00:00:34.076 --> 00:00:35.202
On the surface.

8
00:00:35.285 --> 00:00:37.955
yes. it looks fine. Nice and strong.

9
00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:40.040
But it's not strong at all.

10
00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:41.583
Especially this room.

11
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.293
The roof might fall any second.

12
00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:47.548
That's why repair work needs to be done
as soon as possible.

13
00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:49.550
Stay somewhere else for two weeks.

14
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:51.635
It will be strong after we repair it.

15
00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.429
Okay. whatever.

16
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.931
Fine.

17
00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:57.057
Okay!

18
00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:00.936
In that case. add a window to my room
while you're at it.

19
00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:02.646
What room doesn't have a window?

20
00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.814
Window?

21
00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:04.940
(IN THAI) A window.

22
00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.441
That'll cost more.

23
00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:07.651
MAN 1: Up the price.

24
00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.128
MAN 2: (SPEAKS KOREAN) Korean beef?

25
00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:11.196
- MAN 1: Okay. I like Korean beef.
- Let's eat that.

26
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.364
Okay.

27
00:01:16.285 --> 00:01:19.371
You have to pay triple for the window.

28
00:01:24.418 --> 00:01:25.460
I'm sorry. how much?

29
00:01:26.879 --> 00:01:28.130
(WHISPERS) He's angry.

30
00:01:29.256 --> 00:01:30.632
MAN 1: Pork belly. then.

31
00:01:30.716 --> 00:01:32.384
MAN 2: (IN THAI) Let's eat pork belly.

32
00:01:33.135 --> 00:01:34.335
(IN KOREAN) Just double. then.

33
00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:38.807
All right. fine.

34
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:40.309
(SPEAKS ENGLISH) Nice.

35
00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:41.727
(SPEAKS KOREAN) Thank you. sir.

36
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.520
Thank you. sir.

37
00:01:43.604 --> 00:01:44.980
MAN 3: See you later. sir!

38
00:01:45.063 --> 00:01:46.565
We'll see you in two weeks.

39
00:01:46.648 --> 00:01:47.733
Thank you. sir.

40
00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:52.154
Where do we stay for two weeks?

41
00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:57.701
Jirisan Mountain.

42
00:01:58.452 --> 00:01:59.453
What?

43
00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:04.875
(JINMAN AND JIAN PANTING)

44
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

45
00:02:14.468 --> 00:02:16.303
There's... a cave.

46
00:02:17.638 --> 00:02:18.889
JIAN: Why is there a cave here?

47
00:02:20.224 --> 00:02:21.350
JINMAN: What a relief.

48
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.434
JIAN: That's true.

49
00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:24.686
Be careful.

50
00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:33.987
NO SIGNAL

51
00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:40.661
NO SIGNAL

52
00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:41.995
Darn it.

53
00:02:53.423 --> 00:02:54.842
(JIAN GASPS)

54
00:02:57.928 --> 00:02:58.929
You're too...

55
00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:02.266
You're way too hot!

56
00:03:04.977 --> 00:03:06.603
Once the high fever subsides.

57
00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.940
hypothermia will set in.

58
00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.901
Damn...

59
00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.072
I can't believe I'll get hypothermia
in the mountains at night.

60
00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.198
(SIGHS)

61
00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:20.576
This is ridiculous.

62
00:03:21.243 --> 00:03:22.327
Exactly.

63
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.039
We should've gone to a hotel or a motel.

64
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:28.333
Or some nice and quiet campsite.

65
00:03:28.417 --> 00:03:30.127
Why explore this mountain?

66
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.378
You even hurt your leg!

67
00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.298
That's my hurt leg. (JINMAN GRUNTS)

68
00:03:42.514 --> 00:03:43.765
Listen up. Jian.

69
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:46.560
When you're in a difficult situation.

70
00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.313
instead of arguing over right and wrong.

71
00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.107
it's important to find a way

72
00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:54.234
to solve the problem

73
00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.612
and overcome the situation.

74
00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.238
Okay?

75
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.241
What the heck?

76
00:04:01.742 --> 00:04:03.035
Are you lecturing me now?

77
00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:07.497
We don't even know where we are.

78
00:04:07.998 --> 00:04:08.999
(JINMAN GRUNTS)

79
00:04:13.712 --> 00:04:14.713
What's that?

80
00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:17.716
You had a map?

81
00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:18.967
JINMAN: I think

82
00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:20.886
- this is where we are.
- Okay.

83
00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:25.224
So if you walk
five or six kilometers this way.

84
00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:27.851
there will be a shelter
with an emergency phone.

85
00:04:29.686 --> 00:04:30.687
Can you

86
00:04:31.396 --> 00:04:32.731
get there on your own?

87
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.073
I have to.

88
00:04:42.574 --> 00:04:44.993
You'll become one with Mother Nature
if I don't.

89
00:04:45.077 --> 00:04:46.245
Right.

90
00:04:46.328 --> 00:04:47.579
I love nature.

91
00:04:48.372 --> 00:04:49.665
That wouldn't be so bad.

92
00:04:49.748 --> 00:04:51.416
It sounds good to me too.

93
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.876
I'll get to live on my own.

94
00:04:55.671 --> 00:04:57.714
Right. Jian. Hold on.

95
00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:01.134
Just in case.

96
00:05:01.802 --> 00:05:03.053
take this with you.

97
00:05:04.596 --> 00:05:05.597
(SCOFFS)

98
00:05:06.557 --> 00:05:07.641
What's so funny?

99
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.228
Do you know how many wild boars
are in this mountain?

100
00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.896
What if you run into one?

101
00:05:13.438 --> 00:05:14.773
Wild boars are scary.

102
00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:17.609
If they're hungry and have nothing to eat.

103
00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:19.319
they try to eat humans too.

104
00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:21.071
What are you doing?

105
00:05:21.613 --> 00:05:23.532
Are you trying to scare your rescuer?

106
00:05:24.116 --> 00:05:25.117
Are you scared?

107
00:05:25.909 --> 00:05:26.910
Of course not!

108
00:05:28.078 --> 00:05:30.789
I should run away if I meet a boar.
How will this help?

109
00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:35.669
If you think you're in danger.

110
00:05:36.253 --> 00:05:37.254
shout out my name

111
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.840
at the sky three times.

112
00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:42.593
"Jeong Jinman.
Jeong Jinman. Jeong Jinman!"

113
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:45.179
Then...

114
00:05:46.054 --> 00:05:47.806
I might just show up.

115
00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:51.894
What a load of bull.

116
00:05:54.813 --> 00:05:55.814
Uncle.

117
00:05:56.315 --> 00:05:57.858
I clearly saw you sweat a lot.

118
00:05:58.317 --> 00:05:59.568
Are you sure you're sick?

119
00:05:59.943 --> 00:06:00.944
(COUGHS)

120
00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.780
I'm burning up!

121
00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:06.408
Come on.

122
00:06:07.409 --> 00:06:09.411
Don't you remember when you were little?

123
00:06:10.162 --> 00:06:12.164
When the bullies at school locked you up.

124
00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:14.416
you shouted my name

125
00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:16.710
and I magically appeared.

126
00:06:19.171 --> 00:06:20.464
No. I don't remember.

127
00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.053
Anyway.

128
00:06:26.136 --> 00:06:28.096
leave this if you don't need it.

129
00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.181
Wait!

130
00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:45.239
Wait here.

131
00:06:45.822 --> 00:06:47.699
I'll call for help and be right back.

132
00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.162
Be careful. okay?

133
00:06:52.246 --> 00:06:53.247
Okay!

134
00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:13.600
Hey.

135
00:07:14.893 --> 00:07:16.395
Pasin. it's me.

136
00:07:19.648 --> 00:07:21.233
The drugs are incredible.

137
00:07:26.989 --> 00:07:27.990
Yes.

138
00:07:28.657 --> 00:07:29.992
Jian is on her way down.

139
00:07:32.995 --> 00:07:33.996
Okay.

140
00:07:36.081 --> 00:07:37.749
We should let her decide herself.

141
00:08:07.237 --> 00:08:08.989
Is this the right path?

142
00:08:25.839 --> 00:08:26.840
(BIRDS SCREECHING)

143
00:08:30.427 --> 00:08:32.387
(SIGHS) I found it.

144
00:08:43.023 --> 00:08:44.024
(GASPS)

145
00:09:07.798 --> 00:09:09.341
(DOGS BARKING)

146
00:09:09.883 --> 00:09:10.884
(HYENA SNARLING)

147
00:09:41.707 --> 00:09:42.708
(SCREAMS)

148
00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:57.681
(HYENA SNARLING)

149
00:10:10.652 --> 00:10:12.321
JINMAN: <i>Only the weak bark.</i>

150
00:10:15.782 --> 00:10:17.117
The strong don't.

151
00:10:20.913 --> 00:10:22.122
You must become strong.

152
00:10:23.415 --> 00:10:26.960
<i>Whatever makes you scared.
keep your eyes open and face it.</i>

153
00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:36.386
(DOG WHIMPERING)

154
00:10:43.268 --> 00:10:45.103
(GUNSHOTS)

155
00:10:55.781 --> 00:10:56.782
(SIGHS IN RELIEF)

156
00:11:14.758 --> 00:11:17.261
You were sweating with a fever.

157
00:11:17.344 --> 00:11:18.345
What's going on?

158
00:11:19.221 --> 00:11:20.931
I didn't have to climb down alone.

159
00:11:23.892 --> 00:11:25.936
Nature must've healed me quickly.

160
00:11:26.478 --> 00:11:28.522
I think nature fits me well.

161
00:11:30.315 --> 00:11:31.316
And your leg?

162
00:11:32.901 --> 00:11:34.486
It still hurts.

163
00:11:35.279 --> 00:11:37.072
You saw me limping earlier.

164
00:11:42.786 --> 00:11:45.831
And where on earth
did you get that kind of gun?

165
00:11:47.749 --> 00:11:49.167
It was in the backpack.

166
00:11:49.251 --> 00:11:50.335
Pasin lent it to me.

167
00:11:53.714 --> 00:11:55.591
Why does he have a gun to begin with?

168
00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:00.387
Wait.

169
00:12:02.472 --> 00:12:05.309
So you had a real gun.

170
00:12:07.352 --> 00:12:09.438
but you gave me a slingshot?

171
00:12:09.521 --> 00:12:10.522
(CLEARS THROAT)

172
00:12:12.149 --> 00:12:14.985
What kind of uncle are you?

173
00:12:15.068 --> 00:12:18.447
That's because you don't know
how to use a gun.

174
00:12:20.449 --> 00:12:21.450
(JIAN SIGHS)

175
00:12:40.135 --> 00:12:43.138
(SIREN BLARING IN DISTANCE)

176
00:12:46.642 --> 00:12:50.229
(GUNSHOTS IN DISTANCE)

177
00:13:15.504 --> 00:13:16.505
(GUNSHOT)

178
00:13:28.267 --> 00:13:29.268
A gun?

179
00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:31.144
Where did you get that?

180
00:13:31.979 --> 00:13:33.313
Isn't it illegal?

181
00:13:36.984 --> 00:13:38.277
Do you want to try it?

182
00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:48.495
Listen up. Jian.

183
00:13:49.538 --> 00:13:52.291
Guns are double-edged swords.

184
00:13:53.959 --> 00:13:54.960
With this gun.

185
00:13:55.919 --> 00:13:57.921
you can protect yourself.

186
00:13:59.047 --> 00:14:00.966
and you can save your companions.

187
00:14:02.926 --> 00:14:04.845
But someone always gets killed by it.

188
00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:06.555
Keep that in mind.

189
00:14:09.349 --> 00:14:10.434
This is the magazine.

190
00:14:10.934 --> 00:14:12.144
This is the barrel.

191
00:14:12.895 --> 00:14:14.104
This is the slide.

192
00:14:14.688 --> 00:14:15.772
Inside is the bolt.

193
00:14:15.856 --> 00:14:16.982
Okay.

194
00:14:17.065 --> 00:14:19.401
That's the recoil spring.
and that's the frame.

195
00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:37.669
Align your sights.

196
00:14:38.212 --> 00:14:39.213
Take a deep breath.

197
00:14:39.755 --> 00:14:46.720
A SHOP FOR KILLERS

198
00:14:49.848 --> 00:14:51.892
EPISODE 3
THE STRONG DON'T HOWL

199
00:14:52.267 --> 00:14:54.269
(DRONE WHIRRING)

200
00:15:01.777 --> 00:15:03.779
(DRONE STOPS WHIRRING)

201
00:15:06.073 --> 00:15:07.074
Are you okay?

202
00:15:09.826 --> 00:15:12.120
Jeongmin. snap out of it!

203
00:15:12.204 --> 00:15:13.580
Do you want to die here?

204
00:15:15.207 --> 00:15:17.209
(PANTING)

205
00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:06.091
(IN MANDARIN) Shit.

206
00:16:06.175 --> 00:16:07.676
They've pulled out all the stops.

207
00:16:19.271 --> 00:16:20.939
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

208
00:16:43.504 --> 00:16:45.380
(BOTH GRUNTING)

209
00:17:07.361 --> 00:17:09.571
(GUN BEEPING)

210
00:17:27.965 --> 00:17:31.969
(BOTH GASPING)

211
00:17:36.932 --> 00:17:38.600
This... isn't right.

212
00:17:41.228 --> 00:17:42.312
We have to get out.

213
00:17:48.151 --> 00:17:49.278
Jeongmin.

214
00:18:01.373 --> 00:18:02.374
(BEEPS)

215
00:18:04.918 --> 00:18:05.919
Who are you?

216
00:18:07.171 --> 00:18:10.674
Bae Jeongmin. I... I'm Jian's friend.

217
00:18:19.725 --> 00:18:21.393
What did you just...

218
00:18:40.412 --> 00:18:41.413
Was it you

219
00:18:41.914 --> 00:18:43.248
that tried to kill us?

220
00:18:44.416 --> 00:18:45.417
What's that?

221
00:18:46.835 --> 00:18:47.836
A slingshot?

222
00:19:00.265 --> 00:19:01.642
Let go of me!

223
00:19:02.142 --> 00:19:04.269
Let go! Let go of me!

224
00:19:04.853 --> 00:19:05.854
Let go!

225
00:19:08.148 --> 00:19:11.360
You move without thinking.
You're the opposite of your uncle.

226
00:19:12.027 --> 00:19:15.030
But you better think and move
like your uncle from now on.

227
00:19:15.656 --> 00:19:17.074
If you want to survive.

228
00:19:17.241 --> 00:19:19.159
(GRUNTS AND PANTS)

229
00:19:25.791 --> 00:19:26.792
(GUNSHOT)

230
00:19:52.317 --> 00:19:53.819
SEONGJO: What the hell's going on?

231
00:19:54.403 --> 00:19:56.029
Is someone with her?

232
00:19:56.697 --> 00:20:00.158
Shit. I could've taken her out
with my first shot.

233
00:20:00.242 --> 00:20:01.577
BONGO: Come on. Seongjo.

234
00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.788
If you did that. what's the point
of having all the guys here?

235
00:20:06.081 --> 00:20:07.457
(LAUGHS)

236
00:20:08.125 --> 00:20:09.167
Right?

237
00:20:09.251 --> 00:20:11.545
- I should give them a chance too.
- Of course.

238
00:20:13.005 --> 00:20:14.631
Have this and keep it up.

239
00:20:14.715 --> 00:20:17.092
Let's get something nice to eat
when we're done.

240
00:20:31.023 --> 00:20:32.649
MINHYE: I'm not here to fight you.

241
00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:34.359
I'm here to protect you.

242
00:20:35.027 --> 00:20:36.028
Who are you?

243
00:20:36.612 --> 00:20:38.447
What did you do to Jeongmin?

244
00:20:39.948 --> 00:20:41.325
Don't worry. He's not dead.

245
00:20:44.036 --> 00:20:45.204
Think about it. Jian.

246
00:20:45.787 --> 00:20:47.247
Didn't you find it strange?

247
00:20:47.956 --> 00:20:50.417
"Shout 'Jeong Jinman'
at the sky three times."

248
00:20:54.922 --> 00:20:58.300
You've done it just three times
in the last ten years.

249
00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:01.929
When you were bullied by a girl
in middle school.

250
00:21:02.513 --> 00:21:04.139
when you were sexually harassed.

251
00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.766
and this year.

252
00:21:05.849 --> 00:21:08.894
Your boss at the convenience store
that tried to stiff you.

253
00:21:08.977 --> 00:21:10.687
What happened to them all?

254
00:21:14.399 --> 00:21:15.484
You probably don't know.

255
00:21:15.984 --> 00:21:18.195
but there's a code implanted
in your forearm.

256
00:21:18.946 --> 00:21:21.365
You and your uncle
are the only two green codes.

257
00:21:23.033 --> 00:21:27.287
Whoever received a code has a duty
to protect you. Jeong Jian.

258
00:21:28.872 --> 00:21:31.750
That's why everyone was mobilized
when you shouted his name.

259
00:21:33.001 --> 00:21:35.045
That girl in your class was transferred.

260
00:21:35.671 --> 00:21:38.048
The pervert from college dropped out.

261
00:21:38.715 --> 00:21:40.801
And your boss had an accident. right?

262
00:21:41.677 --> 00:21:42.761
Darn it.

263
00:21:43.262 --> 00:21:44.805
What on earth...

264
00:21:44.888 --> 00:21:46.473
What the hell are you saying?

265
00:21:46.557 --> 00:21:47.850
You saw just now.

266
00:21:47.933 --> 00:21:49.810
the drones trying to kill you.

267
00:21:51.478 --> 00:21:53.146
(MAN OVER PA SYSTEM) <i>I repeat.</i>

268
00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:57.693
<i>Please evacuate to a safe location
as soon as possible.</i>

269
00:21:58.402 --> 00:22:00.779
<i>Let me repeat myself once more.</i>

270
00:22:01.572 --> 00:22:03.740
<i>Until 18:00 hours today.</i>

271
00:22:03.824 --> 00:22:07.160
<i>live firearm training
will be conducted on base.</i>

272
00:22:07.494 --> 00:22:10.622
<i>- It will cause some dust and...</i>
- MAN 1: Even the military is helping.

273
00:22:10.706 --> 00:22:12.624
Seongjo must've pulled some strings.

274
00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.462
All right. let's go if you're ready.

275
00:22:18.881 --> 00:22:22.009
Mr. Kim. it's a house with one girl.

276
00:22:22.092 --> 00:22:23.635
Isn't this overkill?

277
00:22:23.719 --> 00:22:27.306
I know she's Jeong Jinman's niece.
but she's just a 21-year-old kid.

278
00:22:28.056 --> 00:22:29.057
Right.

279
00:22:29.766 --> 00:22:31.977
I hope you're right.

280
00:22:32.644 --> 00:22:33.645
But I don't know.

281
00:22:35.647 --> 00:22:37.232
Team members.

282
00:22:37.316 --> 00:22:39.610
Follow my instructions from now on.

283
00:22:40.903 --> 00:22:41.904
In an emergency.

284
00:22:42.738 --> 00:22:46.074
if you decide to break away and die
from your own judgement.

285
00:22:46.992 --> 00:22:50.829
you'll be departing this life
for chump change

286
00:22:52.122 --> 00:22:55.209
with no insurance and no one to blame.

287
00:22:55.292 --> 00:22:58.086
So keep that in mind and try to keep up.

288
00:22:58.170 --> 00:22:59.505
MAN 2: Yes. sir.
MAN 3: Yes. sir.

289
00:23:02.508 --> 00:23:05.093
One. two. Testing. Mic test.

290
00:23:05.177 --> 00:23:07.137
<i>Seongjo. can you hear me?</i>

291
00:23:08.138 --> 00:23:10.474
Yes. loud and clear.

292
00:23:33.205 --> 00:23:34.665
Don't move and stay there!

293
00:23:51.139 --> 00:23:52.474
SEONGJO: What the hell?

294
00:23:52.558 --> 00:23:54.017
How could that be there?

295
00:23:58.272 --> 00:23:59.398
Jeez...

296
00:24:08.782 --> 00:24:10.117
Hey. it's me.

297
00:24:10.659 --> 00:24:12.452
I think someone's helping the kid.

298
00:24:15.372 --> 00:24:17.374
Damn it. there's too much smoke.

299
00:24:17.457 --> 00:24:20.294
I can't see anything.
Can you clear out the smoke?

300
00:24:20.794 --> 00:24:21.920
Please?

301
00:24:23.505 --> 00:24:25.048
God damn it.

302
00:25:04.046 --> 00:25:05.047
Minhye?

303
00:25:05.631 --> 00:25:07.216
My. my.

304
00:25:19.228 --> 00:25:20.229
(MINHYE GROANS)

305
00:25:31.907 --> 00:25:32.908
Minhye?

306
00:25:37.162 --> 00:25:39.248
This changes everything.

307
00:25:41.416 --> 00:25:42.459
Everyone. wait!

308
00:25:43.377 --> 00:25:45.546
What the hell is Minhye doing there?

309
00:25:45.629 --> 00:25:48.632
MR. KIM: <i>Seongjo? Is that Minhye
in the rabbit hole?</i>

310
00:25:49.383 --> 00:25:51.969
Minhye's Class S
holding Codes Red and Purple.

311
00:25:52.845 --> 00:25:54.930
You'll have to pay more for risk.

312
00:25:55.722 --> 00:25:58.559
Fine. just proceed.

313
00:25:58.642 --> 00:26:00.352
We don't have much time.

314
00:26:01.228 --> 00:26:04.273
Then. I'll trust you and proceed.

315
00:26:05.232 --> 00:26:06.692
- Let's proceed.
- Yes. sir.

316
00:26:07.192 --> 00:26:08.193
Yes. sir.

317
00:26:09.236 --> 00:26:12.155
God damn it. Everyone's all about money.

318
00:26:12.781 --> 00:26:13.782
BONGO: Seongjo?

319
00:26:13.866 --> 00:26:14.992
Who's Minhye?

320
00:26:15.784 --> 00:26:16.785
(SCOFFS)

321
00:26:16.869 --> 00:26:18.579
Just a crazy bitch.

322
00:26:30.924 --> 00:26:31.925
(GRUNTS)

323
00:27:08.629 --> 00:27:10.631
Now. let's begin the rabbit hunt!

324
00:27:13.634 --> 00:27:17.012
Teams 1 and 2 of Group 1
has begun the rabbit hunt.

325
00:27:17.596 --> 00:27:19.389
Fifteen hundred meters to the rabbit.

326
00:27:26.980 --> 00:27:28.482
Come back alive!

327
00:27:47.793 --> 00:27:48.794
- (GUNSHOT)
- (SCREAMS)

328
00:28:14.528 --> 00:28:15.612
JIAN: <i>Focus.</i>

329
00:28:17.739 --> 00:28:19.408
JINMAN: <i>Listen up. Jian.</i>

330
00:28:21.535 --> 00:28:22.536
JIAN: <i>Blind spots.</i>

331
00:29:52.834 --> 00:29:54.711
<i>It's flying in from the left side.</i>

332
00:29:55.379 --> 00:29:56.505
<i>A diagonal direction?</i>

333
00:29:57.089 --> 00:30:01.093
<i>The sound of the gunshot came
from much higher and farther away.</i>

334
00:30:23.657 --> 00:30:24.741
SEONGJO: What?

335
00:30:25.826 --> 00:30:27.744
Where did she go?

336
00:30:31.748 --> 00:30:32.916
- Hey. Bongo.
- Yes?

337
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:34.126
Go forward a bit.

338
00:30:34.209 --> 00:30:35.586
Going forward a bit.

339
00:30:50.851 --> 00:30:51.852
One.

340
00:30:53.729 --> 00:30:54.730
Two.

341
00:30:55.689 --> 00:30:56.690
Three.

342
00:31:02.362 --> 00:31:04.364
(JIAN GROANING)

343
00:31:35.354 --> 00:31:36.730
Have you shot a gun before?

344
00:31:39.858 --> 00:31:40.859
Yes.

345
00:31:42.694 --> 00:31:43.695
Not that one.

346
00:32:03.674 --> 00:32:06.802
When it comes to shooting.
pistols and rifles are the same anyway.

347
00:32:07.386 --> 00:32:10.138
Pull the lever on the right
and insert the bullet.

348
00:32:11.515 --> 00:32:12.766
You just need to load it.

349
00:32:38.333 --> 00:32:39.710
What the fuck?

350
00:32:41.128 --> 00:32:42.337
Look at this bitch!

351
00:32:43.589 --> 00:32:45.966
She's Jeong Jinman's niece indeed!

352
00:32:46.175 --> 00:32:47.176
(LAUGHS MANIACALLY)

353
00:33:08.530 --> 00:33:11.033
I can't believe he stuck a gun
under the sofa.

354
00:33:11.742 --> 00:33:13.660
(IN MANDARIN) That's just like
my dear Jinman.

355
00:33:15.829 --> 00:33:16.830
Your what?

356
00:33:17.664 --> 00:33:20.292
(IN KOREAN) What... do we do now?

357
00:33:27.341 --> 00:33:29.510
The impatient always die first.

358
00:33:34.306 --> 00:33:35.766
God damn it!

359
00:33:35.849 --> 00:33:39.353
Minhye. that bitch.
How much is she getting paid?

360
00:33:52.115 --> 00:33:53.116
MINHYE: There's no time.

361
00:33:53.200 --> 00:33:55.994
I'll cover you. Go into the storage shed.

362
00:33:56.703 --> 00:33:57.871
The storage shed?

363
00:33:57.955 --> 00:34:00.749
Yes. on the floor
of your uncle's workroom.

364
00:34:00.832 --> 00:34:02.584
there's a door into murthehelp.

365
00:34:03.544 --> 00:34:07.256
I'm going to protect you
until you get in there safely.

366
00:34:07.339 --> 00:34:08.632
I promised your uncle.

367
00:34:12.177 --> 00:34:13.428
How can I trust you?

368
00:34:13.929 --> 00:34:15.472
Why should I listen to you?

369
00:34:17.266 --> 00:34:18.350
Aren't you curious

370
00:34:18.851 --> 00:34:20.602
as to who your uncle really was?

371
00:34:32.948 --> 00:34:33.991
Go right now!

372
00:34:55.053 --> 00:34:56.096
SEONGJO: Look at that.

373
00:34:56.930 --> 00:34:57.931
Mr. Kim?

374
00:34:58.682 --> 00:35:01.435
The rabbits are moving
towards the storage shed.

375
00:35:01.518 --> 00:35:04.271
Get a move on. will you?

376
00:35:04.354 --> 00:35:06.815
We just have to go through there.
Can you do it?

377
00:35:07.983 --> 00:35:08.984
Let's go.

378
00:35:14.865 --> 00:35:15.866
(JIAN SCREAMS)

379
00:35:19.578 --> 00:35:20.829
SEONGJO: I knew it.

380
00:35:21.496 --> 00:35:22.706
There it is.

381
00:35:28.504 --> 00:35:29.880
Jeongmin. get up!

382
00:35:44.311 --> 00:35:46.104
(SPEAKS MANDARIN) Got you.

383
00:36:10.295 --> 00:36:11.880
(SPEAKS KOREAN) That little bitch.

384
00:36:17.386 --> 00:36:18.512
Where my uncle worked?

385
00:36:56.341 --> 00:36:57.342
What is this?

386
00:37:00.679 --> 00:37:03.390
What is it? Try his birthday.

387
00:37:04.099 --> 00:37:05.767
His birthday? Birthday...

388
00:37:11.899 --> 00:37:12.900
My birthday?

389
00:37:23.243 --> 00:37:25.162
Damn it! What is it?

390
00:37:25.245 --> 00:37:26.997
Hurry up. Jian!

391
00:37:29.583 --> 00:37:31.001
JINMAN: <i>Listen up. Jian.</i>

392
00:37:31.793 --> 00:37:33.879
It's the same with your school ID number.

393
00:37:33.962 --> 00:37:35.881
2-2-0-1-9-0-7-4.

394
00:37:36.715 --> 00:37:39.134
2-2-0-1-9-0-7-4.

395
00:37:41.637 --> 00:37:42.971
2-2-0-1-9-0-7-4.

396
00:37:53.732 --> 00:37:54.733
It worked.

397
00:39:39.379 --> 00:39:40.422
JEONGMIN: What?

398
00:39:41.298 --> 00:39:42.674
It's really here.

399
00:40:06.073 --> 00:40:07.074
Jian.

400
00:40:07.950 --> 00:40:09.535
- (GUN COCKING)
- (BOTH GASPING)

401
00:40:13.497 --> 00:40:15.374
MAN: Oh... Hi. Jeong Jian.

402
00:40:24.299 --> 00:40:26.176
I'm Brother.

403
00:40:27.302 --> 00:40:32.057
A SHOP FOR KILLERS

404
00:41:13.557 --> 00:41:16.393
(MUFFLED GUNSHOTS)

405
00:41:28.447 --> 00:41:30.449
(INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

405
00:41:31.305 --> 00:42:31.306
